<title>USA: EG&amp;G sees earnings improvements in Q3.</title>
<headline>EG&amp;G sees earnings improvements in Q3.</headline>
<dateline>WELLESLEY, Mass. 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Photographic systems maker EG&amp;G Inc on Wednesday predicted that its performance will improve in the third quarter, possibly approaching last year's $0.30-per-share mark.</p>
<p>EG&amp;G reported a second quarter loss of $0.26 per share, compared with a profit of $0.33 for the year-ago period. The company attributed the earnings downturn primarily to a $0.51 per share after-tax charge prompted by the failure of its IC Sensors division to meet operating plans.</p>
</text>
